# Samsung and Trustonic HIDL interfaces.
#
# None of these were labelled by any policy in this tree, so hwservicemanager
# fell back to default_android_hwservice, which vendor domains may neither add
# nor find. Under permissive that is invisible; under enforcing every Samsung
# HAL that registers one of these interfaces fails and init restarts it in a
# loop - which is what the earlier "camera crash, phone app crash, settings
# crash, call crash" report actually was:
#
#   avc: denied { add } for interface=vendor.samsung.hardware.camera.provider::
#     ISehCameraProvider scontext=u:r:hal_camera_default:s0
#     tcontext=u:object_r:default_android_hwservice:s0 tclass=hwservice_manager
#
# The list below is the full set from /vendor/etc/vintf/manifest.xml rather
# than only the ones that happened to log a denial, so a HAL that registers
# late does not turn into the next bootloop.

